From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:30:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 199/204] security/vboot: Boot on when the TPM fails with mock
 secdata

With VBOOT_MOCK_SECDATA vboot keeps nothing in the TPM, yet a TPM that
does not start makes verstage request recovery (RO_TPM_S_ERROR). On a
board whose read-only part has no recovery path that stops the boot,
which is why VBOOT_MOCK_SECDATA_NO_TPM leaves the TPM to ramstage.
With measured boot the TPM has to start in verstage, and there it only
takes the measurements.

With mock secdata, report the failure and boot on: the measurements
are lost, so the PCRs do not match what the OS sealed to them, but the
machine starts. The same for a TPM that starts but then fails to
extend vboot's PCRs (boot mode, HWID, firmware version), which requests
recovery too (RO_TPM_U_ERROR). The CBFS measurements already only warn.
The mocked secdata spaces are still read, which creates them without
the TPM: left out, as on the error path, vboot finds no valid secdata
and asks for recovery all the same (secdata_firmware: version
incompatible, reason 0x2b).

TEST=QEMU q35 with vboot A/B, VBOOT_MOCK_SECDATA and TPM_MEASURED_BOOT:
without a TPM device, verstage says it boots on without measurements
and the slot boots to the payload (before, without the secdata spaces:
recovery requested, romstage looked for in the read-only CBFS, a hang);
with swtpm, every boot starts the TPM and extends vboot's PCRs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/security/vboot/vboot_logic.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/security/vboot/vboot_logic.c b/src/security/vboot/vboot_logic.c
index 01d43a08cd..7b3bca678f 100644
--- a/src/security/vboot/vboot_logic.c
+++ b/src/security/vboot/vboot_logic.c
@@ -283,7 +283,18 @@ void verstage_main(void)
 		tpm_rc = TPM_SUCCESS;	/* ramstage starts the TPM */
 	else
 		tpm_rc = vboot_setup_tpm(ctx);
-	if (tpm_rc == TPM_SUCCESS) {
+	if (tpm_rc != TPM_SUCCESS && CONFIG(VBOOT_MOCK_SECDATA)) {
+		/*
+		 * No secdata in the TPM: it only takes the measurements. A TPM
+		 * that does not start costs those (the PCRs then do not match
+		 * what the OS sealed), not the boot, and a board without a
+		 * recovery path would stop in recovery mode.
+		 */
+		printk(BIOS_ERR, "TPM setup failed (%#x): booting without measurements\n",
+		       tpm_rc);
+	}
+	if (tpm_rc == TPM_SUCCESS || CONFIG(VBOOT_MOCK_SECDATA)) {
+		/* Mocked, these create vboot's secdata without the TPM */
 		antirollback_read_space_firmware(ctx);
 		antirollback_read_space_kernel(ctx);
 	} else {
@@ -392,11 +403,17 @@ void verstage_main(void)
 		timestamp_add_now(TS_TPMPCR_START);
 		tpm_rc = extend_pcrs(ctx);
 		if (tpm_rc) {
-			printk(BIOS_WARNING, "Failed to extend TPM PCRs (%#x)\n",
-				tpm_rc);
-			vboot_fail_and_reboot(ctx,
-				VB2_RECOVERY_RO_TPM_U_ERROR,
-				tpm_rc);
+			if (CONFIG(VBOOT_MOCK_SECDATA)) {
+				/* As above: the measurements are lost, not the boot */
+				printk(BIOS_ERR, "Failed to extend TPM PCRs (%#x): booting on\n",
+				       tpm_rc);
+			} else {
+				printk(BIOS_WARNING, "Failed to extend TPM PCRs (%#x)\n",
+					tpm_rc);
+				vboot_fail_and_reboot(ctx,
+					VB2_RECOVERY_RO_TPM_U_ERROR,
+					tpm_rc);
+			}
 		}
 		timestamp_add_now(TS_TPMPCR_END);
 	}
